WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.465 --> 00:00:01.647
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.647 --> 00:00:03.434
Today's message is...

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.537
- Change lives.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.868
Over to you, Tim Tebow.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:08.326
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.326 --> 00:00:10.755
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:10.755 --> 00:00:13.583
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:13.583 --> 00:00:17.588
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.588 --> 00:00:19.848
- For me and playing sports,

00:00:19.848 --> 00:00:24.091
it's not being focused on
winning or losing a game

00:00:24.091 --> 00:00:25.528
because, yeah, you want to be the best.

00:00:25.528 --> 00:00:26.695
You want to try to win Super Bowls

00:00:26.695 --> 00:00:28.683
or make it to the Big
Leagues and all these things,

00:00:28.683 --> 00:00:30.597
but you want to, at the end of the day,

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.866
be more than just the sport
you're trying to play.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.703
You want to transcend that sport.

00:00:34.703 --> 00:00:39.467
If all you do, if all I ever
did was win or lose at a game,

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.989
I don't really look at my
life as a lot of significance.

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:44.924
But if I can transcend that
sport to inspire people,

00:00:44.924 --> 00:00:47.827
to put a smile on people's
faces, to encourage people,

00:00:47.827 --> 00:00:48.872
to make a difference,

00:00:48.872 --> 00:00:51.543
to change one person's life
or a million people's lives,

00:00:51.543 --> 00:00:54.127
then I would consider that
significance and meaning.

00:00:54.127 --> 00:00:55.780
The goal is not to be famous.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.518
The goal is not to have
money in your bank account.

00:00:57.518 --> 00:01:00.334
The goal is not to have what
the world defines as a success.

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:01.442
The goal is to change lives.

00:01:01.442 --> 00:01:02.804
- So what do you think?

00:01:02.804 --> 00:01:06.632
- I think it resonates true,
where you're trying to do,

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:07.651
in whatever position you do,

00:01:07.651 --> 00:01:09.911
whether you're doing
something socially or at work

00:01:09.911 --> 00:01:13.981
that you want to see people
around you that look up to you,

00:01:13.981 --> 00:01:16.243
that you inspire, and
take them over the wing

00:01:16.243 --> 00:01:18.805
and never be too tired
to give them more advice,

00:01:18.805 --> 00:01:20.534
be there for them a little more.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:22.810
To move away from your
selfishness, you know,

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.951
"I'm having a bad day" or
"I need to get this done"

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:26.983
and be there for pretty much

00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:29.258
your team and your
friends and your family.

00:01:29.258 --> 00:01:30.712
- Yeah, I think people get into things

00:01:30.712 --> 00:01:32.276
often for the wrong reason.

00:01:32.276 --> 00:01:33.919
I think a lot of people
start a YouTube channel

00:01:33.919 --> 00:01:35.830
'cause they want to be YouTube famous

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.893
and they're only trying to
get a million subscribers.

00:01:37.893 --> 00:01:39.162
I think a lot of people start a business

00:01:39.162 --> 00:01:40.694
just trying to get rich.

00:01:40.694 --> 00:01:43.046
They look at the Forbes magazine

00:01:43.046 --> 00:01:46.065
or the Top 100 Hot Companies
To Start Right Now,

00:01:46.065 --> 00:01:47.736
make a lot of money, and
then they get into it

00:01:47.736 --> 00:01:49.066
and they realize it's a lot harder

00:01:49.066 --> 00:01:50.221
than they thought it was going to be.

00:01:50.221 --> 00:01:51.566
You have to enjoy the process.

00:01:51.566 --> 00:01:52.399
You have to enjoy the work.

00:01:52.399 --> 00:01:53.981
The people who win are on a mission.

00:01:53.981 --> 00:01:56.397
They want to make the
world better somehow,

00:01:56.397 --> 00:01:57.755
whether that's through
your YouTube channel,

00:01:57.755 --> 00:01:59.919
through your business,
through your salsa dancing,

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:00.752
whatever it is,

00:02:00.752 --> 00:02:02.393
you're on a mission that is much more

00:02:02.393 --> 00:02:04.189
than just achieving the end result.

00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:06.485
If you're only chasing result,
you're never going to get there,

00:02:06.485 --> 00:02:08.217
but if you're enjoying the process,

00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:10.097
then success will be yours.

00:02:10.097 --> 00:02:11.804
So the question of the day today is...

00:02:11.804 --> 00:02:13.685
- Have you been there
for someone else today?

00:02:13.685 --> 00:02:15.444
- Have you been there
for someone else today?

00:02:15.444 --> 00:02:16.277
I like it.

00:02:16.277 --> 00:02:17.232
Leave it in the comments below

00:02:17.232 --> 00:02:19.051
and we will join in the discussion.

00:02:19.051 --> 00:02:21.663
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Leong Sai Mun.

00:02:21.663 --> 00:02:23.008
I hope I pronounce it okay.

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:25.075
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:02:25.075 --> 00:02:26.131
Your One Word.

00:02:26.131 --> 00:02:27.787
I really, really, really appreciate it

00:02:27.787 --> 00:02:29.492
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:02:29.492 --> 00:02:30.995
So thank you, guys, so much for watching.

00:02:30.995 --> 00:02:31.828
We believe in you

00:02:31.828 --> 00:02:34.823
and hope you continue
to believe in yourself

00:02:34.823 --> 00:02:36.464
and whatever your one word is.

00:02:36.464 --> 00:02:37.567
Much love.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:39.553
And we'll see you again
tomorrow morning for another...

00:02:39.553 --> 00:02:41.584
- Shot of espresso.

00:02:41.584 --> 00:02:44.294
♫ I wake up every morning

00:02:44.294 --> 00:02:47.835
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:02:47.835 --> 00:02:49.423
(typewriter typing)

00:02:49.423 --> 00:02:52.587
- I think in general you really should try

00:02:52.587 --> 00:02:54.283
to live your life without regrets

00:02:54.283 --> 00:02:58.814
and if you are really set on
starting a particular company,

00:02:58.814 --> 00:03:00.545
even if you know that you could go

00:03:00.545 --> 00:03:02.378
be employee number 30 at Airbnb

00:03:02.378 --> 00:03:06.223
and Airbnb's already going like this,

00:03:06.223 --> 00:03:07.736
and you'd have more of an impact,

00:03:07.736 --> 00:03:09.826
but if you're going to regret
for the rest of your life

00:03:09.826 --> 00:03:11.390
not starting this particular company

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.010
'cause you're so in love with it,

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.117
you might decide to do that.

00:03:15.117 --> 00:03:17.950
However, I think this other thing,

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:21.048
like making an impact on whatever you do

00:03:21.048 --> 00:03:22.644
is sort of the satisfying thing in life,

00:03:22.644 --> 00:03:24.635
in professional life,

00:03:24.635 --> 00:03:28.554
and so I think most people find
that their job satisfaction

00:03:28.554 --> 00:03:30.528
like goes up with the impact they have

00:03:30.528 --> 00:03:32.952
on their company or the world or whatever.

00:03:32.952 --> 00:03:35.869
And if you start a company that is,

00:03:37.302 --> 00:03:39.564
you know, a mild success

00:03:39.564 --> 00:03:41.847
or join a company that's a huge success,

00:03:41.847 --> 00:03:44.639
you probably have more of an
impact in the latter case.

00:03:44.639 --> 00:03:47.200
- The thing which attracted me to Google

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.389
and to internet in general

00:03:49.389 --> 00:03:52.904
is that it's a great equalizer, right?

00:03:52.904 --> 00:03:55.922
And so to me, always
being struck by the fact

00:03:55.922 --> 00:03:58.589
that Google search work the same

00:04:00.461 --> 00:04:03.207
as long as you had access to
computer with connectivity,

00:04:03.207 --> 00:04:04.982
if you were a rural kid anywhere

00:04:04.982 --> 00:04:07.845
or if you were a professor
at Stanford or Harvard.

00:04:07.845 --> 00:04:12.606
And to me, I want Google to
strive to push to do that,

00:04:12.606 --> 00:04:17.400
not just build technology
for a certain segment.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:21.284
For me, it matters that
we drive technology

00:04:21.284 --> 00:04:23.340
as an equalizing force,

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:26.747
as an enabler to everyone
around the world.

